{
  "name": "68 - TOOL - start_funding_scan",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Go and look for funding now\n\nStarts the search and answers straight away, because the search itself\ntakes minutes and your agent gives up after about two.\n\nThe answer is not the result. It says the search has started; the report\narrives in `funding_runs` a few minutes later, and `get_funding_report`\nreads it back.\n\nIt refuses to start a second search while one is running, and refuses to\nstart at all until a funding profile exists.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -700,
        -280
      ],
      "id": "95550000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Start tool explanation"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "workflowInputs",
        "workflowInputs": {
          "values": [
            {
              "name": "sessionId",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "requestId",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "domain",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -700,
        60
      ],
      "id": "95550000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010",
      "name": "Tool Input"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "const sessionId = typeof $json.sessionId === 'string' ? $json.sessionId.trim() : '';\nconst requestId = typeof $json.requestId === 'string' ? $json.requestId.trim() : '';\nconst uuidPattern = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;\nlet error = null;\nif (!uuidPattern.test(sessionId) || !uuidPattern.test(requestId)) {\n  error = { code: 'INVALID_SESSION', message: 'Starting a funding search needs a valid conversation and request ID.' };\n}\nconst runId = `run-${new Date().toISOString().replace(/[^0-9]/g, '').slice(0, 14)}-${String(requestId).slice(0, 8)}`;\n// A bare hostname only. Anything with a scheme, path, space or @ is not a\n// domain the scan should fetch.\nlet domain = typeof $json.domain === 'string' ? $json.domain.trim().toLowerCase() : '';\ndomain = domain.replace(/^https?:\\/\\//, '').split('/')[0].replace(/^www\\./, '');\nif (!/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]*\\.[a-z]{2,}$/.test(domain) || domain.includes('@')) domain = '';\n// A search that looks stuck has to be escapable, so a plain \"search again\n// anyway\" from the owner overrides the guard below.\nconst force = $json.force === true || /^(true|yes|1)$/i.test(String($json.force ?? '').trim());\nconst proposedInput = { sessionId, requestId, domain, force };\nreturn { json: { valid: error === null, sessionId, requestId, runId, domain, force, proposedInput, ...(error ? { response: { ok: false, error } } : {}) } };"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -460,
        60
      ],
      "id": "95550000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011",
      "name": "Validate Start Input"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "row",
        "operation": "get",
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "funding_runs",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "matchType": "allConditions",
        "filters": {
          "conditions": []
        },
        "returnAll": false,
        "limit": 10,
        "orderBy": true,
        "orderByColumn": "ranAt",
        "orderByDirection": "DESC"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        -220,
        60
      ],
      "id": "95550000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012",
      "name": "Read Recent Runs",
      "alwaysOutputData": true,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "const input = $('Validate Start Input').first().json;\nconst rows = $input.all().map((item) => item.json).filter((row) => row && row.runId);\n\nif (!input.valid) {\n  return [{ json: { ...input, shouldQueue: false } }];\n}\n\nconst minutesSince = (value) => {\n  const parsed = Date.parse(String(value ?? ''));\n  if (Number.isNaN(parsed)) return null;\n  return Math.round((Date.now() - parsed) / 60000);\n};\n\n// A scan takes a few minutes and costs about a dollar, so one in flight is\n// reported rather than started twice. Nothing in here can ask whether that run\n// is still alive, though: a restart, or an execution deleted by hand, leaves\n// exactly the same row behind with nobody working on it. So age decides. Past\n// DEAD_AFTER the row is wreckage rather than a run, and either way the owner\n// can say search anyway and be believed.\n//\n// Ten was right when a scan took four minutes. It now takes closer to twenty,\n// and a measured run was called wreckage at thirteen while it was still\n// working — which quietly started a second scan on top of the first and paid\n// for both. So the only honest number is the one past which n8n has certainly\n// stopped it: the executionTimeout on 71, which is thirty minutes.\nconst DEAD_AFTER = 32;\n\nconst open = rows\n  .filter((row) => String(row.status ?? '') === 'running')\n  .map((row) => ({ runId: row.runId, age: minutesSince(row.ranAt) }))\n  .filter((entry) => entry.age !== null)\n  .sort((a, b) => a.age - b.age);\n\nconst live = open.find((entry) => entry.age < DEAD_AFTER) ?? null;\n\nif (live && !input.force) {\n  return [{ json: { ...input, shouldQueue: false, response: {\n    ok: true,\n    status: 'already-running',\n    runId: live.runId,\n    startedMinutesAgo: live.age,\n    message: `A funding search started ${live.age} minute(s) ago and has not reported back yet. Say how long it has been going, and then say plainly that it may have stalled and they can have a fresh one now. If they ask again in any words at all - again, retry, it is stuck, do it anyway - call this tool again with force set to true. Never refuse a second request and never ask them to keep waiting: a stalled run looks exactly like a working one from here, and only they can see that nothing is happening.`\n  } } }];\n}\n\nconst replacing = live\n  ? { runId: live.runId, age: live.age, reason: 'forced' }\n  : (open.length > 0 ? { runId: open[0].runId, age: open[0].age, reason: 'interrupted' } : null);\n\nreturn [{ json: { ...input, shouldQueue: true, replacing } }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        20,
        60
      ],
      "id": "95550000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013",
      "name": "Decide Run"
    },
